<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ur-Nammu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ur-Nammu was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a>, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-sumerian-empire">Neo-Sumerian Empire</a>, who established his rule around 2112 BCE after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>. He is credited with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/code-of-ur-nammu">Code of Ur-Nammu</a>, one of the oldest known law codes, and with major building projects including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziggurat-of-ur">ziggurat of Ur</a>. Accounts of the Neo-Sumerian Empire treat him as the architect of the state's foundation, governance and legacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ur-nammu.jpg" alt="Ur-Nammu" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Steve Harris, source · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Ur-Nammu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
